From 15a08aacaf9322041cdff01daa84c92877cbfca4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DairyOne Agent <agent@dairyone.local>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 07:29:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Phase 1: farmer unavailable/skipped exceptions, dashboard
 next-action + exception count

- trip_exceptions table (farmer_unavailable, farmer_skipped, route_issue,
  other) with RLS mirroring route_deviations.
- Agent can log a per-farmer exception from the trip screen (both the
  current-stop card and the all-stops list); an excepted farmer now
  resolves its stop the same way a collection does, so a genuinely
  unavailable farmer no longer permanently blocks route completion.
- 'Report issue' button on the current stop for route-level/other issues.
- Agent dashboard: next-action subtitle shows the next uncollected
  farmer's name on an active trip, and an open-exceptions count card
  appears when any are logged today.
- Regenerated supabase types.ts from the live schema (was stale --
  missing route_assignments/route_change_requests/route_deviations/
  trip_exceptions).
